Reject too long words in HunspellImpl::checkword

Under HUNSPELL_CHROME_CLIENT, return early for words of MAXWORDUTF8LEN
(UTF-8) or MAXWORDLEN bytes or more. Coverity reported a possible overrun
of a fixed-size buffer here (fixed_size_dest).

diff --git a/src/hunspell/hunspell.cxx b/src/hunspell/hunspell.cxx
index e2cce20..4d0b212 100644
--- a/src/hunspell/hunspell.cxx
+++ b/src/hunspell/hunspell.cxx
@@ -916,6 +916,13 @@ struct hentry* HunspellImpl::checkword(const std::string& w, int* info, std::str
   if (word.empty())
     return nullptr;
 
+#ifdef HUNSPELL_CHROME_CLIENT
+  // We need to check if the word length is valid to make coverity (Event
+  // fixed_size_dest: Possible overrun of N byte fixed size buffer) happy.
+  if ((utf8 && word.size() >= MAXWORDUTF8LEN) || (!utf8 && word.size() >= MAXWORDLEN))
+    return NULL;
+#endif
+
   // word reversing wrapper for complex prefixes
   if (complexprefixes) {
     if (utf8)
